==Strategy==
One hell of an endurance stage consisting of a nasty boss that destroys everything it hits at extreme range, and fast, insanely strong peons that will push with ridiculous powers. For this reason, you will need every cheap, fast, disposable yet powerful attacker as well as defender at your side. A [[Rich Cat]] to start it off and [[Sniper the Cat]] to get Zero Luza off the [[Cat Base]] are highly effective, though you can win without them if you already have all essential units combined with great luck and timing skill (which may still cost many trial-and-error attempts and [[Cat Energy]] due to the [[No Continues]] restriction). Do not hesitate investing in whatever units that may prove helpful, as you'll need to stop and eliminate peons before Luza and the peons head even deeper, and push them back right on time.
*Expect to go out of your way trying to get past this stage, and use whatever units that could be helpful.
*When attempting this on higher difficulties, it's recommended to upgrade any useful [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] to level 50 first to make things easier.
*Don't panic. Zero Luza is a huge threat, but the pressure mostly comes from the peons that come once every so often. If you pay close attention, you could recover ground. Otherwise, even the best strategy can fall on its face.
*Zero Luza's health may seem absurd, but remember its long attack delay allows units to slip in hits.
*The Celeboodles are at a low strength magnification, being there simply to sponsor you with ample amounts of extra cash. [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|Money Up cats]] can exploit them for even more, and would also prove helpful with other peons.
*Bore Jr. is by far the strongest pusher in the entire stage, so utilize a combination of units to try and knock him out quickly before he can beat up your units. Usually, you'll want to send out a hard hitter to immediately deal half of the health, then another one to finish him. Examples of what can fulfill this include Bullet Train Cat, a well-timed Can Can and support to ensure Can Can isn't interrupted (with enough boosts, can be supplemented with an Attack Combo, can even one-shot), Talented Dancer Cat, Doguemon, Teacher BearCat, and Jelly Dumpling (can deal double damage with both direct hit and [[Wave Attack|Wave]]). If you can stall Bore Jr. at least briefly, but enough, you can use a level 46+ Hitman Cat to instantly and consistently 1-shot Bore Jr. each cycle given good enough timing, and some luring if needed (this will also help with the Wild Doges). Idi also works to knock Bore Jr. out. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], especially with his [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]], can eliminate all peons and chip some good damage to Luza in an instant, but his longer recharge means he can't help with all Bore Jr. cycles, so he should just be used to skip an emergency if you're not confident with succeeding, then deal with other crises on your own later until Bahamut is ready again.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] - Can make amazing trades with every enemy in here and clear out the peons effectively, especially Sir Rels, but should be timed well to not die to Zero Luza and should definitely be sent out with other units to not lose too much ground. Still serviceable without the True Form, but will require timing and protection instead of being able to head forth alone, and thus is much less consistent.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] - Provides a moderate damage burst, though not enough to OHKO anything. It's good against any peon, but is best used to snipe certain nasty enemies like Sir Rel, Wild Doge and Bore Jr. in line with other heavy hitters to finish them.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Decent disposable generalist rusher with Long Distance Area Attacks and Behemoth Slayer, the perfect answer to the pesky Wild Doges hiding behind Luza. If supported, can also help in stopping Sir Rels and Relic Doges from advancing.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] - Supercar has a 100% chance to knockback traited enemies with its single-target, short-ranged attack. It can be sent if the peons aren't around to push Luza back, quickly recovering any ground Luza would have gained and thus can play a prominent role. Together with [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] and [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast Cannon]] (Supercar's cooldown is around 18 seconds whereas Doron and Breakerblast both take around one minute), you can keep Luza from reaching your base with ease. Supercar also deals a surprisingly high amount of damage, which can be used to chip Luza as well.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] - Doron has Behemoth and Colossus Slayer, which improves his chip damage against Luza and Wild Doge despite the latter's [[Surge Attack|Surge]] immunity. The ability to knockback and freeze [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] is incredibly powerful, and is essential to recovering lost ground from Luza while Freezing and crippling the Relic peons (though Luza won't be Frozen). Surge adds even more to this and can hit Luza up to 3 times if it spawns at the right spot (otherwise, it'll spawn behind Luza, but another source of Knockback, most easily the Breakerblast cannon, can put Luza into the Surge). As a kamikaze unit that has a rather long recharge time but is undefeated until he attacks, it's best to save him for the waves of Sir Rels to block all enemies and blow them back (his recharge time is definitely enough, but do ensure he doesn't miss his attack).
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - Strong against Relics with 100% chance to Weaken them by 50% for 4 seconds while being Immune to Waves. Colossus and Behemoth Slayer grant Naala a substantial stat boost as well, allowing it to take on most of the threats. Weakening Luza allows your units to survive an otherwise lethal attack (even when Strengthened, as Naala's Long Distance is able to hit Luza by attacking peons) which could make all the difference in battle. Just remember to keep the peons from attacking it too much, as Naala needs all the health to survive one or two more hits from Luza.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] - With full investment in its Move Speed Up talent, Jiangshi Cat is a useful layer of defense. Its guaranteed lethal strike survival can hamper enemy advance somewhat, while keeping Luza in check. However, don't spam it too often if there are no suitable threats around, you'll need the money for important units. If you have Metal Cat, however, Jiangshi may be ignored.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] - A staple in this stage, Metal Macho only takes one damage regardless of how much it was actually struck with, so even Luza will take a while getting past him, and he might be able to hold your line for a few seconds while your attackers remove the peons before Luza could hit your base. Just ensure peons, especially many of them, and even more for Sir Rels, don't overwhelm him.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] - Similar to Metal Cat, but only lasts a little more than a second. Like Doron, though, the enemies won't be able to push through as long as it is there.
*Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - You'll need full Move Speed Up. It's also recommended to boost stats for more influence. A very useful unit to take down nasty peons, later can also chip Luza once peons are exhausted. If used correctly, Can Can is also able to kill Bore Jr.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]/[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - Can delay Luza from range, with Sniper even helping you to keep Luza away, but aside from being vulnerable to peons and Bore Jr.'s [[Mini-Wave]]s, Cyberpunk has a blind spot while Sniper's attack is single-target. You can bring [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]], but that might take some of your precious slots.
*[[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]] - Can survive one pre-Strengthen Luza hit, and stall the Relic peons. Falters when [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] ones come, though, and also replaceable with Maize Cat.
*[[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline/True Superfeline]] - Superfeline is only an option for players with 15001+ [[User Rank]], as that's when its [[True Form]] (which has Colossus Slayer) gets unlocked, or its stats are simply insufficient for its cost. The main appeal of True Superfeline is to wipe out several Relic peons at once with its Omni Strikes (stands at 250, but can hit up to 350 range, and at level 20+80 it does 71k damage, which is enough to cripple the Sir Rels and Relic Doges) while also hitting Luza for some decent chip damage. Its Normal/Evolved Form can be a decent pick here, but only if it's at least level 20+30.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] - This stage solely consists of enemies within this unit's target traits, and he has Behemoth Slayer/Colossus Slayer to counter Wild Doge and Zero Luza, even being able to one-shot the former. Despite his high range for a tank, he can still prove useful in warding off threats from your valuable support units. His other weakness is his high cost due to the cash-tight nature of the stage.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]] - This unit excels in health, movement and recharge speed, with resistance to Relics and Colossus Slayer making it especially suited for countering any Relic enemy in this stage. At level 50, it can survive both of Luza's hits or one Strengthened hit, allowing it to stall the remaining Relics for that much longer. Only downsides are deployment price and how difficult it is to [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|acquire]].
*[[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]] - Brainwashed Flying Cat is Wave-immune and deals massive damage to Traitless. Considering over half the peons are Traitless, this naturally makes them a good pick. A swarm of B.W. Flying Cats can kill Bore Jr. and Wild Doge with extreme ease. This is especially useful considering those two are by far the most annoying and possibly even run-ending peons in the stage.
*Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] - An attacker mainly used to remove Bore Jr., similarly to Brainwashed Flying, but more expensive.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] - A spammable [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] who can deal chip damage onto an unprotected Luza and can beat up the Relic peons well. Be cautious when spamming them though, as these guys can quickly drain your cash and potentially leave you vulnerable to incoming Wild Doges or Bore Jrs.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - Pair him with defenders like Metal Macho or Boulder Cat to consistently handle each Bore Jr. cycle. Can also serve as an instant counter to Wild Doge with proper shielding. Needs extraordinarily precise timing and patience; but when mastered, all 5 Bore Jrs. in this stage becomes trivial to handle. With this, he proves that his egg number: N005, actually represents his Bore Jr. hit count. When attempt this strategy, make sure you can subsequently push Zero Luza back after every Bore Jr. cycle.
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]] - If you are using a sniper like Cyberpunk Cat or Supernova Cosmo, then Mightycat is essential. While he gets crushed by Zero Luza, he can momentarily block Bore Jr.'s Mini-Waves and Weaken him, giving lots of value by protecting your army. His Weaken can also be useful against Wild Doge.
*[[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)|Paperboy Cat]] - If you have managed to clear [[Invasion of Poultrio]], Paperboy Cat will immensely aid in taking down Sir Rel waves and chipping down Zero Luza because of his high speed and incredible burst damage against Relics.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Talented [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] - You'll need his Attack Up, Attack Buff, Defense Buff and Cost Down Talents simply due to how this stage works. Greater Balrog Cat can assist in wiping out the peons (can kill any of them in one hit) to ensure you can stall with ease, while being able to survive just one Luza hit to deliver high damage. If backed with Naala and a Strengthened Luza attacks him while also under the weaken effect, it will only take him a few whacks to kill Luza.
*Talented [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] - Similar story to Balrog as you need levels and the Attack Up Talent. Yukimura is instead used for crippling Bore Jr., ideally before he fires off Mini-Waves to make things easier. Like Bullet Train Cat, you can't send him without a good opportunity. It's also possible to have Yukimura with his Strengthen triggered without dying, causing Bore Jr. to then be killed off immediately and may allow Yukimura to deal some more serious hits.
*[[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]] - Fulfills the exact same role as Immortal Yukimura, but is better suited for this stage overall. With his 100% [[Survive]] ability in True Form, he can survive any attack, even from Zero Luza and net himself additional hits of damage on the boss or annoying peons. If boosted to equal levels (50), this surpasses his original counterpart: Vampiric Yukimura can tank a direct Bore Jr. encounter and retaliate without triggering his Survive ability. This allows him far greater opportunities to damage the boss or other annoying peons than even a Strengthened Immortal Yukimura ordinarily would have.
*Talented [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]] - Mer-Queen Ruri can be a surprisingly effective tank once her Curse Immunity and Target Relic Talents are unlocked. Her resistance and weaken, good damage, combined with her decent recharge, all come into play due to the widespread prevalence of Relic peons. The weaken effect is particularly valuable once Zero Luza Strengthens, as cutting its damage could mean all the difference in battle. However, Ruri is somewhat expensive even for a tank, has single target and will be melted quickly when too many Sir Rels or Traitless peons come by, so make sure to neutralize them quickly.
*Talented [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]] - Similar to Doguemon, it's effective at tanking and clearing out Sir Rels with its powerful Waves, and has Wave Immunity giving it a better advantage at dealing with Bore Jr., but do note that it has the lowest range out of all the tanks previously mentioned and can struggle versus the Traitless peons.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]] - Lasvoss admittedly requires timing and luck to work as Savage Blow is an inconsistent ability and he is very expensive, but he can still deal fairly significant damage if his hits do connect. His talents also help to escalate his destructive power with Colossus Slayer and Move Speed Up.
*[[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-10 Gigapult]] - Gigapult can serve as an efficient stall to Zero Luza if not for a decent period of time, especially for its cost. Its attacks can additionally OHKO Bore Jr. before it even gets a chance to wreak havoc; and similarly to Naala, it can permanently weaken Zero Luza and other relic peons. Beware, however, as Wild Doge and Bore Jr.'s attacks will quickly reduce this mechanical behemoth to nothing but scrap in only a few seconds despite its impressive attack power. If you want to see the most of its value, you will need to defend it with your life while it chips down at Zero Luza, slowly but surely. Defense Buff and Attack Buff Talents are exceptionally useful here.
*Talented [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - Just barely outranges Zero Luza. With his [[Colossus Slayer]] Talent unlocked, he's able to dish out an astounding amount of damage over a long period of time. Even without Talents, he can do tons of damage, and clear peons but will do worse than his Talented version.  Although Zero Luza is [[Immune to Waves]], all other enemies in this stage are not; Supernova Cosmo can consistently clear the stage of peons, leaving Zero Luza to fight all by his lonesome. However, Bore Jr.'s Mini-Waves eat through his entire health pool at record speeds, so be sure to protect him well. When bringing Supernova Cosmo, be careful when using [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]], Breakerblast or Knockback units due to his speed clipping issues.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battle Pod Kozuchimaru]] - With their [[Massive Damage]] against Traitless, they can one-hit kill Bore Jr. and is very easy to land a hit with thanks to their [[Omni Strike]] attack. Just make sure you have enough cash ready when Bore Jr. appears, and the main danger of the stage will be taken care of. After Bore Jr. is dead they will not do much else and will quickly get taken care of by Zero Luza.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]] - His Conjure can Knockback loop Zero Luza with its [[Mini-Surge]]. He's overall an incredible unit and counters pretty much everything in this stage. His only flaw here is if he gets shredded by Bore Jr., which shouldn't be much of an issue if you can save a Conjure to hit each one.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]] - Ultra Kasa Jizo has a guaranteed chance to Survive. This allows him to survive a single hit from Luza as well as deal chip damage to Luza, speeding up the fight. He additionally can help to deal with the peons alongside your other attackers, easing the fight even more.

